Reef: Coral and seabed subtly “alive,” reacting emotionally to events.

SCENE TIMELINE

0.0 – 2.0s | Calm Before
Slow dolly through the filament reef.
The shark glides peacefully past the coral wall. Turtle moves slowly below.
Water threads drift like silk in slow current.

2.0 – 4.0s | Trigger
A low sub-bass hum enters.
The shark’s body begins to blue-shift — filaments tighten, edges sharpen.
Eyes ignite with electric blue light.
Camera pushes in on the eye.

4.0 – 7.0s | Attack
Shark snaps into motion, accelerating unnaturally fast.
Blue filaments ripple like charged cables.
It lunges toward the turtle — mouth opening, filament teeth separating like blades.

7.0 – 9.0s | The Twist
Just before impact, the reef reacts.
Coral filaments surge upward, wrapping around the shark mid-strike.
The turtle remains untouched, motionless — almost indifferent.

9.0 – 12.0s | Consequence
The shark’s blue drains away as the coral absorbs the energy.
Its body unravels into loose, drifting strands — aggression literally deconstructed.
The turtle slowly continues forward.

12.0 – 15.0s | Aftermath
Reef settles. Colors return warmer.
Loose blue filaments dissolve into plankton-like particles.
Final wide shot: harmony restored, but altered.

